      "title": "JEE Main 2023 (11 Apr Shift 2)"
    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is stretched between two clamps <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> apart. The extension developed in the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the fundamental frequency of vibration in the wire will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "80",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using the relation of Young&#39;s modulus,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The linear mass density is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>.</p><p>So,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#961;</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Substituting the values,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>The fundamental frequency is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
